        {
          "name": "two-stops-in-the-same-place-yield-no-direction",
          "why": "A duplicated pole — which the feeds do publish. `atan2(0, 0)` is 0, and 0 is NORTH, so an implementation that just let the maths run would invent a direction and nudge the marker off a kerb it knows nothing about. Answering 0 deliberately is the same “no direction” a one-stop route gets.",
