          "name": "a-stop-beside-the-road-is-snapped-onto-the-line",
          "why": "The reason `line` exists. A bus stop's published coordinate is beside the road — often 10–20 m off, sometimes inside a building — and anchoring a marker there looks fine at a whole-route zoom and falls apart at street level, where the markers scatter off the line they belong to. Each of these sits ~20 m east of a due-north line and every one comes back ON it, with the ROAD's bearing rather than the route's.",
